# Line endings are load-bearing for patches: `git apply` matches context byte by
# byte, and `patches/**` is written and documented as LF. `core.autocrlf=true` is
# what Windows installs by default, so without this rule a checkout of this
# repository would hand back CRLF patch files and every hunk that straddles a line
# break would have to survive on `--ignore-whitespace` alone. Measured before this
# existed: all 75 vendored files were `ASCII text, with CRLF line terminators`.
#
# The same applies to the patches PiCode writes itself: a patch regenerated by
# dev/update_patches.sh must be LF so the next checkout of it still applies.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.patch.no text eol=lf
*.patch.yet text eol=lf

# Shell scripts, so the shebang keeps working when the tree is used from Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
